DESCRIPTION:In 1940\, Newell Convers (N. C.) Wyeth (1882-1945) illustrated 
 scenes for the Anthology of Children's Literature\, a compilation of popul
 ar nursery rhymes\, poetry\, nonfiction\, and more. Wyeth's use of color\,
  perspective\, and figural design made him one of America's foremost illus
 trators. \n Working primarily with pastels\, Harrisburg-based artist Steph
 en Fieser (b. 1955) displays a similar adeptness\, mirroring Wyeth's abili
 ty to play with the relationship between the real and the imaginative. \n 
