SUMMARY:Scott Joplin: The Math and Science of Ragtime
LOCATION:Parkway Central Library
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a Black History Month concert! Engineer and musicia
 n Arjun Ayyangar will perform the music of Scott Joplin\, and discuss the 
 math and science behind the rhythmic syncopation used in the ragtime music
  that Joplin innovated.\n Scott Joplin was "the King of Ragtime Writers\,"
  a composer who elevated "banjo piano playing\," into an American art form
  loved by millions. \n This program takes place in Science Wellness depart
 ment of Parkway Central Library.\n\nhttps://libwww.freelibrary.org/calenda
 r/event/185125
